    <statement><p>Compute the following limits using l'Hopital's rule if appropriate.
Use INF to denote <m>\infty</m> and -INF to denote <m>-\infty</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \lim_{x\to 0} \frac{1-\cos\mathopen{}\left(7x\right)}{1-\cos\mathopen{}\left(6x\right)}</m> =  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \lim_{x\to 1} \frac{7^{x}-6^{x}-1}{x^{2}-1}</m> =  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(\frac{7}{6}\right)^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{7\log\mathopen{}\left(7\right)-6\log\mathopen{}\left(6\right)}{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
